From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ppe: include the exported PPPoE session header in its source

ppe_drv_pppoe_session_deinit() and ppe_drv_pppoe_session_init() are
EXPORT_SYMBOL'd and declared in exports/ppe_drv_pppoe_session.h, but the
translation unit never includes that header, so -Wmissing-prototypes
(6.10) fires.  Include the header rather than repeating the prototypes.
diff -ruN a/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe_session.c b/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe_session.c
--- a/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe_session.c
+++ b/drv/ppe_drv/ppe_drv_pppoe_session.c
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@
 
 #include <linux/netdevice.h>
 #include "ppe_drv.h"
+/* Own exported API: gives the exported functions a visible prototype. */
+#include <exports/ppe_drv_pppoe_session.h>
 
 /**
  * ppe_drv_pppoe_session_deinit
